<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6631" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναισχυντ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναίσχυντος,</span>
			<i>to be shameless, behave impudently,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				460
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				2.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					8.33
				</span></i>
			: also c. part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναισχυντεῖ ποιῶν</span>
			<i>he is impudent enough</i> to do, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				708
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. διαλεγόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Cri.</u>
					53c
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποῖα . . ἀναισχυντοῦσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1383b12
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> trans.,
				<i>treat shamelessly,</i> and 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be so treated,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἀναισχυντῶν πρὸς τὸν
			ἀναισχυντούμενον</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1412a6
			</span></i>.</div>
